  "The Kessler, Walker reason cell spans the page 2 / page 3 boundary: the document prints \"Injury/Illness - Right Lower Leg\" on page 2 and the fragment \"Soreness\" in the player-name position of page 3's first row. The two fragments are joined verbatim (Sorber precedent, 11/15 06:15 AM snapshot) and the row is flagged; no other cell on the row is altered.",
